          "wheel": {
            "at": [
              0.5,
              0.5
            ],
            "dy": -240,
            "n": 6
          }
        },
        {
          "wait": 1500
        }
      ],
      "why": "Milky Way and Andromeda tearing into tidal tails, 100k-star N-body on the GPU.",
      "label": {
        "zh": "星系相撞 · 40 亿年后",
        "en": "GALAXY COLLISION · 4 BILLION YEARS FROM NOW"
      },
      "note": "Scrubbing .gcx-time snaps the camera to a far wide view and the galaxies stay apart (probed 400-900): do NOT scrub. Let it play at 2x from load; tune the wait so the record lands on the tidal-tail moment. Tested: at ~20s wait the merger is happening but small/dim in frame; added a wheel zoom-in — verify scale, or crop with ss:2. After zoom (tested): merger reads as a dim star cloud, not yet premium — try the 俯视 camera, a longer/shorter wait, or demote.",
      "mode": "step"
    },
